      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the separator system</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">is a component in an electrochemical cell having a positive electrode and a negative electrode; wherein at least one surface of any of the first high mechanical strength layer, the second high mechanical strength layer, the third high mechanical strength layer and the fourth high mechanical strength layer has a surface roughness such as a surface roughness characterized by a rms selected from the range of 1 nm to 1000 nm, providing a space for an electrolyte between the first high mechanical strength layer, the second high mechanical strength layer, the third high mechanical strength layer or the fourth high mechanical strength layer and the positive electrode or the negative electrode of the electrochemical cell.</span>
