        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0066">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the first electronically and ionically conductive layer</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">comprises a Au, Al, Cu, Ti, Zn, Ag, stainless steel, Li, Sn, Si, Ni, steel, Tungsten, Tin, Lead, Constantan, Mercury, Germanium or any of their alloys, graphite, carbon black, graphene, carbon nanotubes, coke, Li alloys, Fe alloys, Indium tin oxide (ITO), lanthanum-doped strontium titanate (SLT), yttrium-doped strontium titanate (SYT), Poly(fluorene) s, polyphenylenes, polypyrenes, polyazulenes, polynaphthalenes, Poly(acetylene) s, Poly(p-phenylene vinylene), poly(pyrrole) s, polycarbazoles, polyindoles, polyazepines, polyanilines, poly(thiophene) s, poly(3,4-ethylenedioxythiophene), poly(p-</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0066">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the first electronically and ionically conductive layer</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">comprises a porous or perforated material having a porosity greater than or equal to 30%, greater than or equal to 40%, greater than or equal to 50%, greater than or equal to 60%, greater than or equal to 70%, greater than or equal to 80%, greater than or equal to 90%, selected from the range of 30% to 90%, selected from the range of 40% to 80%, selected from the range of 50% to 70% or selected from the range of 50% to 90%.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0067">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the first electronically and ionically conductive layer</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">comprises a chemically resistant material, a heat resistant material, a mechanically resistant material or any combination of these.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0068">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the first electronically and ionically conductive layer</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">comprises a thin film structure deposited on at least one external surface of the separator, the positive electrode or the negative electrode.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0068">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the first electronically and ionically conductive layer</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">comprises a coating coated on at least one external surface of the separator, the positive electrode or the negative electrode.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0068">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the first electronically and ionically conductive layer</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">has an electronical conductivity greater than or equal to 1 S/cm, greater than or equal to 10 S/cm or greater than or equal to 100 S/cm.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0069">
