      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">a mechanically, chemically and/or heat resistant layer</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">that is ionically and electronically conductive positioned adjacent to the positive electrode permits use of cathode materials that expand and contract during charging/discharging, as a secondary conductivity path for current collection is provided by this layer which may route electrons to the cathode current collector.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0229">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
